---
<Guest title="Hot Tub">
  <p>Relax in the outdoor spa — your personal mountain retreat.</p>

  <h2>The Basics</h2>
  <ul>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li><strong>Location:</strong> rear covered deck outside the living room slider</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li><strong>Maximum occupancy:</strong> six guests</li>
    <li><strong>Water temperature:</strong> pre-set to 102°F (adjustable)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before Your First Use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Remove the spa cover completely before entering</li>
    <li>Check water temperature</li>
    <li>Never use the spa alone</li>
    <li>No glass containers near the spa</li>
    <li>Supervise children at all times</li>
    <li>Shower before your first use</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Towels available in the hallway linen closet</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Operating the Spa</h2>

  <h3>Power</h3>
  <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><p>The spa should already be running. Find the control panel on the side facing the deck stairs.</p>

  <h3>Temperature</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Press "Temperature" or "Temp"</li>
    <li>Use +/- to adjust (recommended 100–104°F)</li>
    <li>Allow 30–60 minutes for change</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Jets</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Main jets:</strong> cycles through low / medium / high / off</li>
    <li><strong>Air controls:</strong> physical valves on the spa rim</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Lights</h3>
  <p>Press "Light" to turn on / off. Press again to cycle colors.</p>

  <div class="g-callout">
    <p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> leave the spa in standard mode. Don't turn it off in winter — it can damage the equipment.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Safety Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Maximum 15–20 minutes per session</li>
    <li>Do not use after drinking alcohol</li>
    <li>Consult a doctor if pregnant or with health concerns</li>
    <li>Do not exceed 104°F</li>
    <li>Children require constant adult supervision</li>
    <li>Use caution on wet deck surfaces</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Exit immediately if you feel:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Dizzy or lightheaded</li>
    <li>Nauseous</li>
    <li>Excessively fatigued</li>
    <li>Overheated</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Winter Use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The spa stays heated year-round — extra magical in the snow</li>
    <li>Always replace the cover after use (prevents freezing)</li>
    <li>Watch for ice on the deck</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Using the Cover</h2>

  <h3>Removing</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Unclip the locks on the front</li>
    <li>Lift one side and fold back</li>
    <li><strong>Never drag the cover</strong> — it will damage it</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Replacing</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Center the cover over the spa</li>
    <li>Lock all clips securely</li>
    <li>Always secure the cover when not in use</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What's Provided</h2>
  <ul>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Clean towels in the hallway linen closet</li>
    <li>Spa net for debris removal</li>
    <li>Test strips (optional)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to Bring</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Swimsuit</li>
    <li>Drinking water</li>
    <li>A towel for walking back inside</li>
    <li>A robe (optional)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Don'ts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No glass containers</li>
    <li>No oils or bath products</li>
    <li>No food in the spa (beverages OK — no glass)</li>
    <li>Don't adjust chemical levels yourself</li>
    <li>Don't remove any equipment</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

  <h3>Not heating?</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Confirm it's on at the control panel</li>
    <li>Check the temperature setting</li>
    <li>Allow time — can take hours</li>
    <li>Contact the property manager if it persists</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Error code on display?</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Note the code</li>
    <li>Try resetting: turn off for 30 seconds, turn back on</li>
    <li>Contact the property manager with the code</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>Water cloudy?</h3>
  <p>Contact the property manager immediately. Do not use until cleared.</p>

  <h2>Before You Leave</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Ensure the spa cover is securely fastened</li>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER --><li>Place used towels in the bathtub or shower</li>
    <li><strong>Leave the spa running</strong> — we'll handle shutdown</li>
  </ul>

  <p style="margin-top: 32px;">Questions? See <a href="/guest/contacts">Contacts</a>.</p>
</Guest>
